</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results on Other Baselines.</span> We evaluate our two-stage framework based on Qwen-3b <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, and the results are reported in Tab. <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table A6 ‣ A.4 More Ablation Studies ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ FineRS: Fine-grained Reasoning and Segmentation of Small Objects with Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A6</span></a>. As observed, employing a smaller backbone leads to noticeable performance degradation, particularly on small objects. Nevertheless, our method still surpasses SegZero <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> under the same backbone configuration, demonstrating its superior adaptability and robustness.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
